ORDINANCE IV OF 2012
ESTABLISHMENT OF THE SINDH MEDICAL UNIVERSITY ORDINANCE, 2012
An Ordinance to provide for the establishment of
the University known as the Sindh
Medical University
at Karachi.
[Gazette of Sindh, Extraordinary, Part I,
4th June, 2012]
No.Legis:
1(4)/2012, dated 1-6-2012.---The following Ordinance
made by the Governor of Sindh is hereby published for
general information.
Preamble.---Whereas it is expedient to provide for the
establishment of the University known as the Sindh
Medical University at Karachi and to provide for the matters connected
therewith or ancillary thereto.
And whereas the
Provincial Assembly is not in session and the Governor is satisfied that
circumstances exist which render it necessary to take immediate action;
Now, therefore, in exercise of the powers conferred by clause (1) of
Article 128 of the Constitution of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan, 1973, the
Governor is pleased to make and promulgate the following Ordinance:---
CHAPTER I
PRELIMINARY
2. Definitions.---In this
Ordinance, unless there is anything repugnant in the subject or context---
(a) "Academic
Council" means the Academic Council of the University;
(b) "affiliated
college" means the college affiliated to the University but not maintained
or administered by it;
(c) "affiliated
institute" means an institute affiliated to the University but not
maintained and administered by it;
(d) "Authority"
means any of the Authorities of the University specified in section 23;
(e) "Chancellor"
means the Chancellor of the University;
(f) "college"
means a constituent college or affiliated college imparting instructions or
practical training in courses of studies relating to health sciences and allied
sciences;
(g) "Commission"
means the Higher Education Commission;
(h) "constituent
college" means a college maintained and administered by the University;
(i) "constituent institute" means an institute maintained
and administered by the University;
(j) "Dean" means
the head of Faculty;
(k) "Director" means
the head of a institute;
(l) "Faculty"
means a Faculty of the University;
(m) "Government"
means the Government of Sindh;
(n) "honorary
Professor" a Professor who provides academic service on honorary basis;
(o) "Officer" means
any of the officer of the University specified in
section 9;
(p) "prescribed"
means prescribed by statutes, regulations or rules;
(q) "Principal"
means the head of a constituent or affiliated college;
(r) "Pro-Chancellor"
means the Pro-Chancellor of the University;
(s) "Professor
Emeritus" means a retired Professor working in the University;
(t) "Pro-Vice
Chancellor" means the Pro-Vice Chancellor of the University;
(u) "registered
graduate" means a graduate of the University who has his name entered in
the register maintained for the purpose;
(v) "Registrar"
means the Registrar of the University;
(w) "Senate" means
the Senate of the University;
(x) "statutes",
"regulations" and "rules" means respectively the statutes,
the regulations and the rules made under this Ordinance;
(y) "Syndicate"
means the Syndicate of the University;
(z) "teachers"
means teachers engaged as Professor, Associate Professors, Assistant Professors
and Lecturers and such other persons as may be declared to be teachers by
regulations;
(aa) "Teaching Department" means a
Teaching Department established and maintained or recognized by the University;
(bb) "University"
means the Sindh
Medical University,
Karachi;
(cc) "Vice-Chancellor"
means the Vice-Chancellor of the University; and
(dd) "visiting teacher" means a
teacher who is invited for
teaching by the University for a short period;

Officers of the University

